{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/665577-gentry-and-mantles","id":665577,"title":"Gentry and Mantles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-15T05:52:47-07:00","id":665577,"title":"Gentry and Mantles","content":"Feel kinda weird starting a thread for such a short topic, but I suspect the answer might be somewhat subjective. Basically - do you guys think it would make sense for a member of the Gentry to have a Mantle if they do strongly identify with the stuff the court is themed around? Given that Gentry have access to Court contracts - some of which add Mantle to the dice pool - I kinda find myself wondering if a Gentry whose realm was one of eternal winter or spring might have Mantle... despite, as mentioned, almost certainly not being part of a court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T06:21:39-07:00","id":665629,"title":"","content":"Sure, having a mantle would not break a game and they certainly could have a contract with one of the four seasons. Still, the biggest benefit is related to the various courts and access to contracts. The rest are mostly descriptive. A Fae of winter does not need a mantle to have an aura of cold or a contract of winter. They after all deal directly with Winter and don't need to the court to mediate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T08:09:41-07:00","id":665752,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the concern is less for fluff reasons, and more for the actual crunch. A lot of the court-specific contracts use Mantle as part of the dice pool, and as per... I'm pretty sure it was Equinox Road where it explicitly says they can gain court contracts- but yeah, as those contracts use Mantle as part of the activation, it seems... a bit weird that the embodiments of the Wyrd that are the Gentry can't gain that full dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T09:46:34-07:00","id":665821,"title":"","content":"The Contracts' primary purpose in their writing was for PC use. They likely just saw better use for the wordcount than describing what to do for NPCs who would logically have identical/similar powers, but may not get at them the same way. Just having the NPC wind up using it with an appropriate dice pool is the way to go. In this case, I'd probably just rule something like, &quot;This Gentry has a clear resonance with this power, and therefore has a functional Mantle rating of X (probably 5) for the purposes of this or these abilities.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:53:44-07:00","id":666001,"title":"","content":"There's no reason to actually give a Mantle to a True Fae given that the Titles they collect are basically superior versions of Changeling's lesser Mantles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:00:01-07:00","id":666010,"title":"","content":"Those titles don't add to the dice pools to active court contracts, and there's a certain logic in a Fey with an eternal kingdom of winter being particularly... influential on Changelings of the Winter Court. So I'd personally disagree with that statement. I'm more concerned about whether there are reasons that a member of the Gentry could have their strong association with a season and emotion represented with the Mantle merit. Given the mention of hermits from the court gaining the merit, and yet garnering respect by virtue of their commitment to what the mantle represents, it doesn't seem entirely implausible, but it's very likely I've missed something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:48:43-07:00","id":666047,"title":"","content":"1) Those Titles add to Wyrd, and I also don't see a reason why they shouldn't add in for Mantle if someone wants to run it that way. I don't think it's too much to say that they fill the same function on relevant matters.<br /> <br /> 2) I don't think the Winter Court, who's entire MO is &quot;Run the fuck away from the True Fae&quot;, would approach <i>any </i>True Fae, no matter how many icicles are hanging from their nose.<br /> <br /> 3) Which, by the way, points the flaw in the comparison. Mantles are a product of the Freehold's Story(Yes, even in 1st Edition, the logic applies), and the basis for these courts and freeholds is &quot;Keep the Strangers away&quot;. I have no problem letting Titles fill in for Mantle and even mimicking the effects of Mantles, but from the game's metaphysics it makes no sense for the True Fae to have a weaker version of a significant portion of their metaphysical makeup that's explicitly Wyrd-bound to a core idea of <i>rejecting</i> the True Fae itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:24:21-07:00","id":666443,"title":"","content":"So is your suggestion that effective mantle in any given court should be equal to the number of Titles? I mean- The thing is, I don't quite understand why you're so opposed to representing that tie with a merit that grants both a bonus to activate certain contracts and gives some actually quite thematic bonuses. I'm not suggesting it has the same fluff, but - for example - the one and five dot Spring mantle bonuses are both pretty apt. While it certainly wouldn't stem from the same contracts with the seasons - in fact, as mentioned, it's likely a property of their titles - many of the mechanical benefits seem apt, and your suggestion doesn't allow for... any flexibility, if that makes sense? They'd be just as good at activating Winter Court contracts as Spring ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T02:19:41-07:00","id":666634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/665577-gentry-and-mantles?p=665752#post665752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the concern is less for fluff reasons, and more for the actual crunch. A lot of the court-specific contracts use Mantle as part of the dice pool, and as per... I'm pretty sure it was Equinox Road where it explicitly says they can gain court contracts- but yeah, as those contracts use Mantle as part of the activation, it seems... a bit weird that the embodiments of the Wyrd that are the Gentry can't gain that full dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not see this wierd ( or <b>wyrd</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). The True Fae that embodies cold and winter is not really in contact with THE WINTER the same way as Winter Court. Seasonal Courtiers are <b>servants</b> for the Season, Pledge with it and loyal to the Season - Gentry is only using Season as cloak they wear on Sundays ( the same applies to other kinds of Courts ).<br /> <br /> Also, remember that Gentry still will have large Activation Dice Pools, with their inhuman stats - <i>Contracts of Stone</i> are still easier to use when you have Strength 7-8 than changelings 3-4 with Mantel 2-3, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-17-2015, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T04:33:34-07:00","id":668071,"title":"","content":"I mean, that's fair. I guess a Wyrd 8-9 Changeling being better at activating Court contracts kind of shows their connection with... mortal emotion and the mortal world? I could get behind the Gentry having relative trouble with that, due to a relationship with the mortal realm along the lines of &quot;Is Mayonnaise a season&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}